{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U1p8ikw5eAZ9LpeAkKHVkg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tcontract: 22\n2\t# Stack profile — the only place in the pipeline that knows how this project builds and tests.\n3\t# The gate and the pre-commit hook read it; a command that is not declared is skipped and named.\n4\t\n5\tcompile: ./gradlew testClasses\n6\ttest: ./gradlew test --rerun\n7\te2eTest: ./gradlew test-e2e --rerun\n8\tbrowser: playwright\n9\t# One more test source set: the gate picks the command that covers the file a mapped test\n10\t# lives in, so `src/test-integration/java` needs its own entry.\n11\ttest.integration: ./gradlew test-integration --rerun\n12\thttp.stub: wiremock\n13\tfilterFlag: --tests\n14\tfilterFormat: \"{class}.{method}\"\n15\tarchitecture: ./gradlew test-architecture\n16\tformat: ./gradlew spotlessCheck\n17\tformatFix: ./gradlew spotlessApply\n18\t\n19\t# The one source a stage may treat as an authority. Generated from the same sources as the\n20\t# building blocks and the rule catalog this project consumes.\n21\tknowledge: dca-knowledge\n22\tknowledge.read: guide/language-mappings/building-blocks.md\n23\t\n24\t# Who carries a stage's craft and a review perspective. A skill works in every agent tool; an\n25\t# agent only where the tool has agents, and the stage then falls back to its own description.\n26\tcarrier.build: dca-modelling\n27\tcarrier.guard: dca-discipline\n28\tcarrier.glossary: ubiquitous-language\n29\tcarrier.domain: context-map\n30\tcarrier.test: e2e-testing\n31\treview.ddd: review-ddd\n32\treview.hexagonal: review-hexagonal\n33\treview.clean-code: review-clean-code\n34\treviews: dca\n35\treview.dca: dca-audit\n36\t\n37\t# Where the project keeps its map; glossaries are the per-context glossary.md files.\n38\tcontextMap: docs/architecture/context-map.md\n39\t# What must hold for any change (story-gate.py --change, the commit hook, CI). The end-user suite\n40\t# needs a running shop, so it