log operations.\nsrc/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductPageController.java:112:    model.addAttribute(\"message\", \"Welcome to the Product Catalog\");\nsrc/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java:33:    return new ProductCatalogPageViewModel(items, items.size(), \"Product Catalog\");\nsrc/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/inventory/events/StockInitializationTrigger.java:10: * (Product Catalog) implements this interface on its event. This way the Inventory module listens\nsrc/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/inventory/adapter/incoming/event/StockInitializationEventConsumer.java:16: * The producing module (Product Catalog) implements this interface on its {@code\nsrc/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/cart/application/shopping/additemtocart/AddItemToCartUseCase.java:65:    // Remote-capable read (Product Catalog via ACL) - outside the transaction","numLines":19,"totalLines":19},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012pNZFVuK5NAU12YFAVY3CX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxzCTo5XjswahLkpoqxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PywwHQ1REC3T1MRrNTDsb4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/product/epics/browse-catalogue/CAT-01/story.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":39449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbb8aca7-514f-4f1a-a705-cb8042c61239","uuid":"80d2a8b2-84fe-4dfd-a69b-816d6a7fb4e8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:38:13.219Z","request_id":"req_011CfxzCTUEtJfo551RFMJPq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PywwHQ1REC3T1MRrNTDsb4":{"file_path":"/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/product/epics/browse-catalogue/CAT-01/story.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PywwHQ1REC3T1MRrNTDsb4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tid: CAT-01\n3\tepic: browse-catalogue\n4\tstatus: delivered\n5\tdelivered: 2026-09-26T06:36:21Z\n6\tdelivered_by: gate\n7\tcontext: product\n8\ttitle: The catalogue lists the range\n9\tdepends_on: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t# The catalogue lists the range\n13\t\n14\t## Story\n15\t\n16\tAs a visitor I want to see every product the shop sells on one catalogue page, in an order that does not\n17\tchange between visits, so that I can find out what the shop offers without asking.\n18\t\n19\t## Acceptance criteria\n20\t\n21\t<!-- happy-path: catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range -->\n22\t\n23\t### Rule: The shop starts with its sample catalogue\n24\t\n25\t#### catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range\n26\t- Given the shop has started and seeded the sample catalogue of `seed-catalogue.json`\n27\t- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n28\t- Then it shows 21 product cards\n29\t\n30\t### Rule: Products are listed by name, compared character by character\n31\t\n32\t#### catalogue-is-in-name-order\n33\t- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n34\t- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n35\t- Then the card titles are in ordinal order of the product name\n36\t- And the first card is `\"Bounded Context\" Enamel Pin`\n37\t\n38\t### Rule: A card shows what the product is\n39\t\n40\t#### card-shows-name-description-and-image\n41\t- Given the seeded product \"Domain-Driven Design\"\n42\t- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n43\t- Then its card shows the name \"Domain-Driven Design\", its description and its image\n44\t\n45\t#### card-leads-to-the-product\n46\t- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n47\t- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n48\t- Then every card offers a \"View Details\" link to that product's page\n49\t\n50\t### Rule: The page is recognisable as the catalogue\n51\t\n52\t#### catalogue-page-heading\n53\t- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n54\t- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n55\t- Then the page title is \"Product Catalog\", the heading reads \"Our Products\" and the breadcrumb reads \"Home / Products\"\n56\t\n57\t## Out of scope\n58\t\n59\t- The price on a card — `PRC-01`, from the price owner.\n60\t- The \"In Stock\" / \"Out of Stock\" badge — `AVL-01`.\n61\t- The product page behind \"View Details\" — `CAT-02`.\n62\t- The initial shown for a product without an image: every seeded product has one; a product without an image\n63\t  can only be created through the API — `shop-api`.\n64\t- A catalogue with no products: the shop always starts with its sample catalogue, so the empty page is not\n65\t  reachable from outside.\n66\t\n67\t## Notes\n68\t\n69\t- Shared scenario: `scenario.catalog.seeded-in-name-order`.\n70\t- Inventory: product P1, P3, P4 (name, description, image and link part).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbb8aca7-514f-4f1a-a705-cb8042c61239","uuid":"9ffce00b-80e1-43c5-8361-61cfd2aa4109","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:38:13.237Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/product/epics/browse-catalogue/CAT-01/story.md","content":"---\nid: CAT-01\nepic: browse-catalogue\nstatus: delivered\ndelivered: 2026-09-26T06:36:21Z\ndelivered_by: gate\ncontext: product\ntitle: The catalogue lists the range\ndepends_on: []\n---\n\n# The catalogue lists the range\n\n## Story\n\nAs a visitor I want to see every product the shop sells on one catalogue page, in an order that does not\nchange between visits, so that I can find out what the shop offers without asking.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n<!-- happy-path: catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range -->\n\n### Rule: The shop starts with its sample catalogue\n\n#### catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range\n- Given the shop has started and seeded the sample catalogue of `seed-catalogue.json`\n- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n- Then it shows 21 product cards\n\n### Rule: Products are listed by name, compared character by character\n\n#### catalogue-is-in-name-order\n- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n- Then the card titles are in ordinal order of the product name\n- And the first card is `\"Bounded Context\" Enamel Pin`\n\n### Rule: A card shows what the product is\n\n#### card-shows-name-description-and-image\n- Given the seeded product \"Domain-Driven Design\"\n- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n- Then its card shows the name \"Domain-Driven Design\", its description and its image\n\n#### card-leads-to-the-product\n- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n- Then every card offers a \"View Details\" link to that product's page\n\n### Rule: The page is recognisable as the catalogue\n\n#### catalogue-page-heading\n- Given the seeded sample catalogue\n- When a visitor opens the catalogue page\n- Then the page title is \"Product Catalog\", the heading reads \"Our Products\" and the breadcrumb reads \"Home / Products\"\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The price on a card — `PRC-01`, from the price owner.\n- The \"In Stock\" / \"Out of Stock\" badge — `AVL-01`.\n- The product page behind \"View Details\" — `CAT-02`.\n- The initial shown for a product without an image: every seeded product has one; a product without an image\n  can only be created through the API — `shop-api`.\n- A catalogue with no products: the shop always starts with its sample catalogue, so the empty page is not\n  reachable from outside.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Shared scenario: `scenario.catalog.seeded-in-name-order`.\n- Inventory: product P1, P3, P4 (name, description, image and link part).\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PywwHQ1REC3T1MRrNTDsb4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
