{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxzDdynvN4KpawBJyza3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0171efAFEv2ivf9cz88TqaE9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/.dca-factory/runs/catalogue-title/plan.md","content":"# Plan — catalogue-title\n\n## Context\nProduct context, feature `catalogue` (`product/spec/product/catalogue/scenarios.md`). Adopt mode: `status: adopted` — the shop already titles the catalogue page; nothing is built, no production code or existing test changes.\nCarrier: in-session, `dca-modelling` not needed — adopt mode names no domain element.\n\n## Changes\n| Element | Kind | Location | New or changed | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| none — adopt mode | — | — | — | story front matter `status: adopted` |\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog  →  level: e2e — Playwright (`./gradlew test-e2e`), happy path\n\n## Where the behaviour lives\n| Key | Behaviour | Covered by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog | `src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java:33` sets \"Product Catalog\"; `ProductPageController.java:71` puts it as `title`; `src/main/resources/templates/layout.pug:7` renders it | `src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/CatalogTitleE2ETest.java` — `CatalogTitleE2ETest.catalogPageIsTitledProductCatalog` |\n\n## Spec delta\n- adds catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog\n\n## Invariants\n(none — adopt mode changes no domain type)\n\n## Files\n- `src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/CatalogTitleE2ETest.java` — read: the existing test that covers the criterion\n- `src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java` — read: where the title is set\n\n## Open assumptions\n- The title is also asserted under CAT-01's `catalogue-page-heading` (`product/spec/product/catalogue/scenarios.md:36`, `src/test-integration/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java:108`); this story adds its own key so both shops hold the same spec (story Notes, WP-107). The overlap is a finding for the spec's owner, not resolved here.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":46315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":549},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbb8aca7-514f-4f1a-a705-cb8042c61239","uuid":"c24663e3-8576-49ec-8922-fb21b09dc7d8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:38:35.927Z","request_id":"req_011CfxzDdcDAn6wGtYxj5wNR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0171efAFEv2ivf9cz88TqaE9":{"file_path":"/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/.dca-factory/runs/catalogue-title/plan.md","content":"# Plan — catalogue-title\n\n## Context\nProduct context, feature `catalogue` (`product/spec/product/catalogue/scenarios.md`). Adopt mode: `status: adopted` — the shop already titles the catalogue page; nothing is built, no production code or existing test changes.\nCarrier: in-session, `dca-modelling` not needed — adopt mode names no domain element.\n\n## Changes\n| Element | Kind | Location | New or changed | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| none — adopt mode | — | — | — | story front matter `status: adopted` |\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog  →  level: e2e — Playwright (`./gradlew test-e2e`), happy path\n\n## Where the behaviour lives\n| Key | Behaviour | Covered by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog | `src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java:33` sets \"Product Catalog\"; `ProductPageController.java:71` puts it as `title`; `src/main/resources/templates/layout.pug:7` renders it | `src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/CatalogTitleE2ETest.java` — `CatalogTitleE2ETest.catalogPageIsTitledProductCatalog` |\n\n## Spec delta\n- adds catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog\n\n## Invariants\n(none — adopt mode changes no domain type)\n\n## Files\n- `src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/CatalogTitleE2ETest.java` — read: the existing test that covers the criterion\n- `src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/web/ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java` — read: where the title is set\n\n## Open assumptions\n- The title is also asserted under CAT-01's `catalogue-page-heading` (`product/spec/product/catalogue/scenarios.md:36`, `src/test-integration/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java:108`); this story adds its own key so both shops hold the same spec (story Notes, WP-107). The overlap is a finding for the spec's owner, not resolved here.\n"}}}
