ue-title`, and both gates passed.\n\nThis story is an adopted one: the shop already titles the catalogue page \"Product Catalog\", so neither stage wrote or changed any code or test.\n\n- **Plan** (`.dca-factory/runs/catalogue-title/plan.md`): the one criterion, `catalogue-tab-reads-product-catalog`, is at level `e2e` and is marked as the happy path. The title is set in `ProductCatalogPageViewModel.java:33`, passed to the page as `title` in `ProductPageController.java:71`, and rendered by `layout.pug:7`. The spec delta adds the criterion to `product/spec/product/catalogue/scenarios.md`.\n- **Test** (`.dca-factory/runs/catalogue-title/tests.md`): the criterion maps to the existing `CatalogTitleE2ETest#catalogPageIsTitledProductCatalog`, which already passes. Its display name matches the scenario's title word for word, and its assertion is at line 18. No characterization test or break patch was needed.\n\nI didn't run the formatter, because no source file changed.\n\nOne overlap is recorded in the plan's open assumptions: CAT-01's `catalogue-page-heading` criterion already asserts the same title, in `ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java:108`. This story adds a separate criterion for it so the Java and .NET shops share the same spec (WP-107). Whoever owns the spec should decide whether to keep both.","ttft_ms":1715,"type":"result","duration_ms":130043,"uuid":"10d81a4e-90a9-4902-bb0e-ae13afa1a477","ttft_stream_ms":1429,"time_to_request_ms":135,"first_content_frame_ms":1429,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
